  "id": "Hounslow-P_2026_0126",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Proposed construction of a full-length rear dormer roof extension to provide an additional bedroom and a bathroom at loft level.\nThe dormer will be set back a minimum of 600mm from the neighbouring property boundary and a minimum of 500mm from the existing eaves, in order to minimise visual impact and protect neighbouring amenity. The ridge height will be retained, with a minimum distance of 300mm maintained between the existing ridge line and the new dormer roof, ensuring the dormer remains subordinate to the host roof and is not visible from the front elevation.\n\nIn addition, 2 rooflights (Velux-style) windows are proposed on the front roof slope to provide natural daylight to the loft accommodation. The proposed development has been designed to respect the character and appearance of the existing dwelling and the surrounding area, while providing improved internal accommodation.",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed hip-to-gable roof extension would disrupt the symmetry of the semi-detached pair, resulting in an unbalanced and visually discordant appearance that harms the character of the dwelling and wider streetscene. The rear dormer, due to inadequate side offsets and excessive span, would create an overly bulky and dominant roofscape that undermines the proportions of the host property. The proposal fails to comply with Local Plan policies CC1, SC7 and the Residential Extension Guidelines under Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD."
